  "prefLabel": "Plc 504.01 Advertising by Approved Providers Allowed",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 504.01 Advertising by Approved Providers Allowed. An approved provider may advertise its approved status and that it is an appropriate vehicle for any licensee who:\n\n(a) Has been directed to participate in a professionals’ health program by a disciplinary order from, or agreement with, an applicable board;\n\n(b) Wishes to propose to an applicable board that participation in a professionals’ health program be considered by the applicable board in disposing of pending or potential disciplinary actions; or\n\n(c) Wishes to obtain assistance via an NKTB path.\n\nSource. #13971, eff 7-1-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc500.html"
